Package: dynMPE
Type: Package
Title: Dynamic Marginal Policy Effects in Thresholding Designs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aditya", "Ghosh", email = "ghoshadi@stanford.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Stefan", "Wager", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the dynamic marginal policy effect of a threshold rule,
    the effect on long-run discounted outcomes of marginally moving the cutoff
    of a policy that is applied repeatedly to the same units, using the
    twice-discounted local linear regression of Ghosh and Wager (2025)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2512.15244>. The bandwidth is chosen by a dynamic
    version of the Imbens and Kalyanaraman (2012) rule, standard errors are
    cluster-robust by unit, and confidence intervals use the bias-aware
    critical value of Armstrong and Kolesar (2020).
